Title: PreToolUse hook — warn when Write/Edit targets the main repo path during a worktree session
Created: 2026-05-23
Author: HDMX-coding-agent

--- log ---
2026-05-23T14:25Z HDMX-coding-agent created — wasted edit + main-repo revert during worktree session in aedist-technical-report

--- body ---
## Context

During an `EnterWorktree` session, `Write`/`Edit`/`Read` accept any absolute path.
An edit to `/home/haduong/<repo>/<file>` lands in the **main repo**, not the
worktree — the project rule `.claude/rules/workflow.md` ("Worktree paths") warns
about exactly this, but nothing enforces it.

On 2026-05-23 a `Write` to `<repo>/.github/workflows/CI.yml` (instead of the
worktree-rooted path) silently edited the main repo's working tree. It was caught
only because a later `uv` parse read the *worktree* copy and mismatched. Cost: one
wasted edit, plus a `git restore` to clean the stray modification off main.

This is a class of error (any agent, any session), high-frequency in worktree-heavy
workflows, and the failure is silent — the write succeeds, just in the wrong tree.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A `PreToolUse` hook (matcher: `Write|Edit|NotebookEdit`) fires when a worktree
      session is active AND the tool's `file_path` resolves under the primary repo
      root rather than the active worktree root.
- [ ] On match it WARNS (declarative, non-blocking by default) with the corrected
      worktree-rooted path, e.g. "path resolves to main repo; did you mean
      <worktree>/<relpath>?". Per workflow.md, hook output must be declarative, not
      an imperative "INSTRUCTION:" (the model classifies imperative hook text as
      prompt injection and ignores it).
- [ ] No false positive when the path is already inside the active worktree, or when
      no worktree session is active (hook is a silent no-op).
- [ ] First test: feed the hook a synthetic PreToolUse payload (main-repo path while
      a worktree is active) on stdin and assert the warning is emitted; feed a
      worktree-rooted path and assert silence. Pure stdin/stdout, no real git state.

## Guidance

- Detect "worktree session active" the same way `erg-pr-merge:in_worktree()` does:
  `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` != `git rev-parse --git-dir`. The active worktree
  root is `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` from the session cwd; the primary repo root
  is the parent of `--git-common-dir`.
- Decision to make during Plan: warn-only vs. block (`exit 2`). Lean warn-only first —
  blocking risks false positives on legit cross-repo edits (the env has additional
  working dirs). Revisit if warnings prove insufficient.
- Scope the matcher to write tools only; never gate `Read` (read-from-main is
  sometimes intentional).
- Wire via `settings.json` hooks, not a skill (this is automatic behaviour).

Sibling from same session: [[0170]] (erg-pr-merge --delete-branch). No dependency.
